{{!--
  Replaces tauri-bundler's built-in template, for two things it does not do:
  `%F`, so a folder dropped on the launcher is opened the way `sanity <path>`
  opens one, and `MimeType`, so sanity is offered under a file manager's Open
  With for a directory, which is how somebody would actually reach for it.

  Reached through `bundle > linux > deb > desktopTemplate`. That is named for
  the Debian bundle but is the only desktop file template there is: the
  AppImage bundler lays out a Debian data tree and takes this file out of it.

  `categories` is `bundle > category`. A custom template replaces the default
  whole, so two things it provides have to be kept by hand here: the
  `StartupWMClass`, without which the running window does not group under its
  own icon, and, should `fileAssociations` ever be added, the `MimeType` it
  would otherwise contribute.

  Handlebars comments rather than `#` ones: this file is the source, and the
  reasoning above belongs to whoever edits it rather than in every copy that
  ships inside a bundle.
--}}
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name={{name}}
{{#if comment}}
Comment={{comment}}
{{/if}}
Categories={{categories}}
Keywords=repository;git;code;canvas;monitor;
Exec={{exec}} %F
StartupWMClass={{exec}}
Icon={{icon}}
Terminal=false
MimeType=inode/directory;
